-- responsive: the base Script for a thing's fixed `responses`. A thing
-- that extends the `responsive` atom of the Base EDL answers from them:
--
--   responses {
--     target: { take: "It's bolted to the floor." }
--     room: { say: "The silence swallows your words." }
--     veto: { beforeAdd: "The floor is too hot." }
--   }
--
-- `target`, `indirect` and `room` refuse a Verb when the thing is offered
-- it in that role; `veto` vetoes a `before…` Decision. A thing's own Script
-- is asked first, and may pass to these.

on any message m
  put the args of m into args
  if the length of args is 2 and kindOf(item 1 of args) is "text" then
    put the optional (the name of m) of the optional (item 1 of args) of the responses of the target into reply
    if kindOf(reply) is "text" then
      return {refused: reply}
    end if
  end if
  pass any message
end any message

-- a Decision's fixed veto
function vetoFor event
  put the optional (event) of the optional veto of the responses of the target into reply
  if kindOf(reply) is "text" then
    return reply
  end if
  return nothing
end vetoFor

on beforeRemove actor, subject, deciding
  if vetoFor("beforeRemove") is not nothing then
    veto vetoFor("beforeRemove")
  end if
  pass beforeRemove
end beforeRemove

on beforeAdd actor, subject, deciding
  if vetoFor("beforeAdd") is not nothing then
    veto vetoFor("beforeAdd")
  end if
  pass beforeAdd
end beforeAdd

on beforeExit actor, subject, deciding
  if vetoFor("beforeExit") is not nothing then
    veto vetoFor("beforeExit")
  end if
  pass beforeExit
end beforeExit

on beforeEnter actor, subject, deciding
  if vetoFor("beforeEnter") is not nothing then
    veto vetoFor("beforeEnter")
  end if
  pass beforeEnter
end beforeEnter
